# RU-First UI Localization (Sprint 42.5)

## Rule

A new screen **must not** ship to Production with any English user-facing string
(except brand/model acronyms: AI, CRM, ERP, API, MCP, JWT, OAuth, OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Telegram, WhatsApp).

## Required

- Use `term()` / `localizeLabel()` / `builderDisplayName()` from `@/i18n/platformGlossary`
- Use `bu()` from `platform-builder/i18n/builderUiRu` for builder chrome
- Put shared terms in `platformGlossary.ts` (alias `platformGlossary.ru.ts`)

## Forbidden

```tsx
// ❌
<Button>Create</Button>
<h1>Dashboard</h1>
title="Coming Soon"

// ✅
<Button>{term("create")}</Button>
<h1>{term("dashboard")}</h1>
title={term("comingSoon")}
```

## Never auto-replace short English tokens in source

Do **not** global-replace `Create`, `Type`, `Name`, `Preview`, etc. inside the codebase —
this corrupts identifiers and HTTP headers (`Content-Type`).

## Gate

Before merge of UI work:

```bash
cd src/web && node scripts/localization_audit.mjs
```

Critical surfaces (Concierge, AI Builder, AI Team, Framework, glossary) must report:

- English strings: 0
- Hardcoded English: 0
- Missing translation: 0
- Localization coverage: 100%
